{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Toulouse who ruled the County of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as count of Tripoli at the age of 12 and was placed under the regency of his mother.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father was killed in 1152 by the Hashshashin in a surprise attack on the castle of Nephin. Raymond III succeeded his father as count of Tripoli at the age of 12 and was placed under the regency of his mother. Hodierna was a powerful and influential woman who played a significant role in the early years of Raymond III's reign.\n\n*Reign*\nRaymond III came of age in 1155 and took control of the government of Tripoli. He faced numerous challenges during his reign including conflicts with the Byzantine Empire and the Hashshashin. In 1156 Raymond III was forced to sign a treaty with the Byzantine Emperor Manuel I Comnenus recognizing Byzantine suzerainty over Tripoli. He also had to deal with the growing power of the Hashshashin who were a major threat to the county.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin and Later Life*\nIn 1187 Raymond III was one of the leaders of the Crusader army that was defeated by Saladin at the Battle of Hattin. He escaped from the battle and fled to the city of Tyre. Raymond III died in 1187 and was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35264554619789124}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.814704541582614e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logpr